Description: Redis-compatible distributed database, multi-master and leaderless
 Mimir is a distributed database for a cluster of trusted machines that
 speaks the Redis protocol. A client connects to any node, over RESP2 or
 RESP3, and every command works whichever node it talks to: every write
 commits by agreement on a majority of the cluster, with no leader and no
 central coordinator. Valkey 8's command documentation is its specification.
 .
 This package holds mimir-node, its systemd unit and its settings. The
 service is installed disabled: review /etc/mimir/config.yaml and
 /etc/mimir/secrets.yaml, then enable mimir.service.
